  "factor_definition": {
    "name": "intraday_half_session_extreme_shock_reversal_completion_2h",
    "direction": "higher",
    "formula": "Within each independent 120-close half-session form 119 adjacent log returns. Choose the earliest index k attaining the maximum absolute return, let s be that return, and let R=log(last_close_in_half/close_immediately_after_s). Define h=-2*s*R/(s^2+R^2). Return the arithmetic mean of the morning and afternoon h values.",
    "economic_hypothesis": "Prompt directional retracement of the largest one-minute shock in both continuous half sessions is consistent with liquidity replenishment and completed price discovery rather than persistent inventory pressure, potentially leaving a more resilient close-known state for the next-open-to-third-close horizon.",
